    {
      "_id": "itbGzYPsod0RdUQc",
      "_key": "!actors.items!LHNGfSXq09KzdTlk.itbGzYPsod0RdUQc",
      "name": "Lycanthropy (Magical Curse)",
      "img": "icons/magic/symbols/runes-carved-stone-green.webp",
      "effects": [],
      "sort": 900,
      "ownership": {
        "default": 0
      },
      "flags": {},
      "type": "feat",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<p>Any Humanoid that fails its saving throw against the Bite attack of a lycanthrope becomes cursed with Lycanthropy. A cursed creature suffers the following effects:</p><p><strong>Forced Transformation.</strong> Each day at dusk, if the full moon is out, the cursed creature makes a DC 12 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the creature transforms into a lycanthrope of the same type as the one that cursed it, losing its game statistics and gaining the statistics of the lycanthrope. The GM controls the creature, which is stuck in its Hybrid Form and can't use its Shape-Shift Bonus Action. This transformation lasts until dawn.</p><p><strong>The Beast Within.</strong> When a creature transformed by the Forced Transformation effect kills another creature, the transformed creature makes a DC 10 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, it loses a part of itself to the curse. On a success, the DC of subsequent saving throws against this effect increases by 1. For each time the creature has failed this saving throw, the DC of Forced Transformation increases by 2. When the DC of Forced Transformation becomes 20, the creature loses itself to the curse entirely, becoming an NPC under the GM's control and permanently assuming the statistics of the lycanthrope.</p><p><strong>Fighting the Curse.</strong> Initially, a <em>Remove Curse</em> spell is enough to cure the curse. After a creature has failed the saving throw against The Beast Within at least once, the <em>Greater Restoration</em> spell or similar magic is necessary. After the transformation becomes permanent, a <em>Wish</em> spell or similar magic is necessary to remove the curse and return the creature to its original form.</p><p><strong>Spreading the Curse.</strong> While transformed into a lycanthrope, the creature is capable of cursing other creatures with its Bite attack.</p>",
          "chat": ""
        },
